      "writtenOn": "2022-03-25T13:40:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why only for connected sockets? The current (TCP) callbacks only require that the socket be bound, not that it be connected. Cn we do the same here? Seems like better behaviour would be:\n\n- If the socket is not bound, EX_TYPE_FILTER_SOCKET_NOT_BOUND\n- If the socket is bound to a different address than the one in the QosSocketInfo, EX_TYPE_FILTER_SOCKET_LOCAL_ADDRESS_CHANGED.\n- If the QosSocketInfo has no destination address, succeed (EX_TYPE_FILTER_NONE).\n- If the QosSocketInfo has a destination address, and the socket doesn\u0027t have a destintion address, EX_TYPE_FILTER_SOCKET_NOT_CONNECTED.\n- If the QosSocketInfo has a destination address, and the socket\u0027s destination address is different, EX_TYPE_FILTER_SOCKET_REMOTE_ADDRESS_CHANGED).\n\nand we could do this for both TCP and UDP.\n\nAssuming we agree that that is the desired behaviour, we need to think about whether this changes the behaviour for TCP, and if so, whether there will be any backwards compatibility implications for existing clients.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 104,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 104,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "55c70679818647f5ce04b6b17e403e4d374cd7ea",
