      "message": "I know that getLocalAddressFromFileDescriptor already does this, but this should never happen, right? QosSocketInfo can never have a null fd because its constructor would throw. Or is this in case the getFileDescriptor$() call there returns null? But wouldn\u0027t that just not work at all?\n\nCan we remove these null checks? If we can\u0027t remove them in all cases, can we at least prevent things from being null in some cases (e.g., never allow null in T+, or never allow null in T+ or for UDP sockets, or...)?",
